{
 "_about": "Models local-model can download for the PC's graphics card (or a Mac's), read by windows/local-model.ps1, unix/local-model.sh and the panel. Grouped by model; each size is in its newest version. Each file's SHA-256 is pinned: a file that changes on Hugging Face is refused until it's checked again here. kind: official = from the maker's own page; quantized = the maker's model, converted to GGUF by a well-known uploader; uncensored = changed by someone outside the maker's team (refusals removed). card_gb / mac_gb: the memory a size needs on a graphics card / a Mac, with an 8,000-token conversation. default: the model local-model picks when none is named (its largest size that fits the card). tested: run on the RX 5700 XT (8 GB) with UVMC's tools (docs/design.md 7i). Made by hand-picked lists and the sizes and hashes read off Hugging Face on 2026-11-10.",
 "default": "qwen",
